## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to securely manage per-tenant TLS credentials in a CNF gateway, including secret-driven config, hot-reload of TLS material, and per-tenant mTLS verification.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes Secrets mounted as TLS material for sidecars
- Hot-reload of TLS credentials without pod restart
- Mutual TLS with per-tenant CA certificates
- Rotation cadence, error handling, and tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo example: load TLS certs from mounted files and reload on change
let tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
  ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
  key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
});

// watch secret mount and refresh TLS context
fs.watch('/mnt/cnf-tls', () => {
  tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
    ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
    cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
    key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate certificate expiry and revocation in this flow?
- What are the trade-offs between in-cluster secret rotation vs external secret management (e.g., Vault) for CNF gateways?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests resilience‑oriented CNF design for multi‑tenant traffic, focusing on per‑tenant state, timing windows, and safe recovery

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant state tracking within a sidecar
- Rolling window counters and cooldown handling
- 503 responses during open state, then auto‑recover

## Code Example
```javascript
class Breaker {
  constructor() { this.map = new Map(); }
  allow(tenant) {
    const s = this.map.get(tenant) || {f:0, t:0, open:0};
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now < s.open) return false;
    if (now - s.t > 60000) { s.f = 0; s.t = now; }
    const ok = s.f < 5;
    if (!ok) s.open = now + 30000;
    this.map.set(tenant, s);
    return ok;
  }
  fail(tenant) {
    const s = this.map.get(tenant) || {f:0, t:Date.now(), open:0};
    s.f += 1; s.t = Date.now(); this.map.set(tenant, s);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to test the breaker under load? Probe metrics and simulate bursts
- How to persist breaker state across restarts? Serializable store
- How to tune thresholds for different tenants?

